        <p class="profile-detail-region">Life · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Alexander the Great</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">356 BCE – 323 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">Probably 20 July 356 BCE (the exact date is uncertain) at Pella, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>; son of King Philip II of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argead-dynasty">Argead dynasty</a> and his fourth wife, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olympia">Olympias</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">10 or 11 June 323 BCE in the palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, aged 32, after an illness of about twelve days; the ancient accounts differ on its course, and some alleged poison</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>, 336–323 BCE; Hegemon of the League of Corinth and commander of the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> from 336 BCE; crowned in the temple of Ptah at Memphis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>; ruler of the conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Persian Empire</a>; the battles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-issus">Issus</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaugamela">Gaugamela</a> and the Hydaspes; never losing a battle; founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and more than twenty other cities; the spread of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-language">Greek language</a> and culture and the beginning of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a>; the legends gathered in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-romance">Alexander Romance</a></span></div>
        </div>
